[H1]How to Choose:

[H2]Option 1: Install All Architectures
Select the "All Architectures" option at the top of the menu to install
ROCm components for all available GPU architectures. This is the largest
installation but ensures compatibility with any GPU in the system.

[H2]Option 2: Install Specific Architecture
If you know your GPU model, find it in the list above and select the
corresponding gfx architecture for a smaller, optimized installation.

Examples:
  RX 7900 XTX: Select gfx1100
  MI300X: Select gfx942
  MI455X: Select gfx1250
  Ryzen AI 9 HX 370: Select gfx1150
  Radeon PRO V710: Select gfx1101
  Ryzen AI Max+ 395: Select gfx1151
  RX 6700 XT: Select gfx1031
  Radeon VII: Select gfx906

If unsure about your GPU model, after installation run 'rocminfo' or
'amd-smi' to verify your GPU's exact gfx architecture code.

[H1]Usage:
Use Up/Down arrows to navigate. Family headers (Instinct:, Radeon PRO:, etc.)
are automatically skipped during navigation.

Press Space or Enter to select your GPU architecture.
Press DONE when finished to return to the ROCm Options menu.

[H1]Auto-Detection:
If you don't select a GPU architecture manually, the installer will attempt
to auto-detect your GPU and install the correct components automatically.
